{
  "description": "Phase 3 agent evaluation. Natural-language questions with expectations defined BEFORE evaluation: acceptable tool sets, argument constraints (checked after schema normalisation), answer checks (each must_include_any group needs one match, case-insensitive), grounding facts (must appear in the answer AND in tool evidence) and citation requirements. fake_plan is used only by the deterministic fake-model mode, which measures orchestration and validation, not LLM quality.",
  "version": 2,
  "created": "2026-11-26",
  "changelog": [
    "v1 (2026-11-26): original expectations used for the fake-model and real-model runs (Stage 1, Phase 3C).",
    "v2 (2026-11-26, Phase 3D): R07 'grounding_facts' [\"photovoltaic\"] replaced by concept groups (a correct paraphrase may not use that word); R09 and A31 scored by the abstention check (valid phrase AND no further claims) instead of a phrase list. Original real-model scores are unchanged; saved answers re-scored offline are stored separately."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {"id": "R01", "category": "exact_structured", "question": "Who won the 2022 Nobel Prize in Chemistry?",
